>     items_url = f'https://api.zotero.org/groups/{group_id}/collections/{collection_key}/items'
>     all_items = []
>     start = 0
>     limit = 100  # You can adjust this limit up to 100 (the maximum Zotero allows)
> 
>     while True:
>         params = {'start': start, 'limit': limit}
>         items_response = requests.get(items_url, headers=headers, params=params)
> 
>         if items_response.status_code == 200:
>             items = items_response.json()
>             if not items:  # If no more items, exit the loop
>                 break
>             all_items.extend(items)
>             start += len(items)  # Move to the next set of items
>         else:
>             print(f'Error retrieving items for collection {collection_key}: {items_response.status_code}')
>             break
> 
>     for item in all_items:
>         print(f'Title: {item.get("title", "No Title")}, Category: {parent_category}')
> ```
> 
> ### Summary of Changes
> 
> 1. **Pagination Logic**: The `get_collection_items` function now prepares to handle multiple pages of items by including the `start` and `limit` parameters.
> 2. **Accumulating Items**: It collects all items from the collection into the `all_items` list before printing them out, ensuring you see all items rather than just the first 25.
> 3. **Error Handling**: If any API call fails, it will print an error message without causing the entire program to crash.
